@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Reference / design method. Native Git/OO/data notation illustration, not a commitment to advanced product features.
title Proposed / illustrative — Normalization walkthrough with explicit example dependencies
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "UNNORMALIZED teaching relation\nResume(resumeId, title, ownerId, ownerName,\n repeating entries[entryId, entryLabel, position])" as U
rectangle "1NF flat teaching relation\nSelection(resumeId, entryId, position, title,\n ownerId, ownerName, entryLabel)\nCandidate key: (resumeId, entryId)" as N1
rectangle "2NF\nResume(resumeId PK, title, ownerId, ownerName)\nEntry(entryId PK, entryLabel)\nSelection(resumeId PK/FK, entryId PK/FK, position)" as N2
rectangle "3NF\nOwner(ownerId PK, ownerName)\nResume(resumeId PK, title, ownerId FK)\nEntry(entryId PK, entryLabel)\nSelection(resumeId PK/FK, entryId PK/FK, position)" as N3
U --> N1 : remove repeating group; atomic values for this example
N1 --> N2 : remove partial key dependencies
N2 --> N3 : remove ownerName transitive dependency
note bottom of N2
 Assumed example functional dependencies:
 resumeId -> title, ownerId
 ownerId -> ownerName
 entryId -> entryLabel
 (resumeId, entryId) -> position
 No other dependencies or alternate keys asserted.
end note

@enduml
